{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - MFA - Okta MFA Factor Deactivated, Suspended or Reset",
	"Description": "An MFA factor was deactivated, suspended, or reset. Any of the three leaves the account with less second-factor coverage than it had a moment ago; correlate with what signed in afterwards.\n\nEvent types: user.mfa.factor.deactivate, user.mfa.factor.suspend, user.mfa.factor.reset_all, user.mfa.factor.update\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/sigmahq/sigma/identity/okta/okta_mfa_reset_or_deactivated/\n- https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/identity/okta/okta_mfa_reset_or_deactivated.yml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "bd3672bc-d401-52f3-a940-17b8a20be055",
